{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Oppose requests for an apology for Britain\u2019s historical role in slavery",
        "additional_details": "Today\u2019s British population bears no responsibility for slavery centuries ago. We believe an apology is unjustified.\r\n\r\nSlavery was a global injustice, but Britain later led efforts to end the trade. William Pitt argued for abolition, and the Royal Navy helped suppress the international slave trade.\r\n\r\nWe feel that our history should acknowledge both Britain\u2019s involvement and its leading role in abolition, without imposing guilt on today\u2019s population.\r\n",
        "background": "We call on the Government to refrain from issuing an apology on behalf of the present British population for Britain\u2019s historical involvement in slavery.\r\n\r\n",
